Maintainer: Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: zyphoros-settings-xfce
Architecture: all
# What the settings name: the panel's plugins (a missing one makes the panel
# ask to remove it), the themes, fonts and the login screen; the wallpaper
# diverted from xfdesktop4-data and linked to desktop-base's.
Depends: x11-common,
         xfdesktop4-data,
         desktop-base,
         xfce4-panel,
         xfce4-whiskermenu-plugin,
         xfce4-pulseaudio-plugin,
         xfce4-power-manager-plugins,
         xfce4-notifyd,
         greybird-gtk-theme,
         elementary-xfce-icon-theme,
         fonts-noto-core,
         fonts-noto-mono,
         lightdm,
         lightdm-gtk-greeter,
         zyphoros-artwork,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Zyphor OS defaults for the Xfce desktop
 The look and layout of Zyphor OS's Xfce edition: one bottom panel with the
 Whisker menu, window buttons, tray, sound, battery, notifications and
 clock; the Greybird theme with elementary icons and Noto fonts; the
 desktop-base wallpaper; default applications; and the LightDM login screen
 in the same style.
 .
 The settings live in /etc/xdg/zyphoros-xfce, which Xfce sessions read
 before /etc/xdg (see /etc/X11/Xsession.d/56zyphoros-xfce), so they only
 change defaults: a user's own choices in ~/.config always win, and
 Debian's files are left untouched.
